 "reading": "Power = chance the check passes when the true mean paired difference equals the column value. For the primary set of 82 cases (what remains after the blind mapper on the extended corpus): at true difference 0 the check passes 97 times in 100; at -0.02, 89; at -0.04, 67; at -0.06, 41; at -0.08, 16. With the spread widened by 25 percent the figure at 0 falls to 89. For the 60-case corpus first prepared (54 primary) the same figures were 89, 75 and 54. By the normal approximation, 80 percent power needs about 40 cases if the true difference is 0, about 63 if it is -0.02, and about 77 if it equals the v7 point estimate of -0.029. Adding repetitions does not help (the unit is the case); adding cases does. The protocol therefore states in advance that a lower bound below -0.10 is reported as FAIL on the preregistered rule and is read as not proven, not as a measured loss."
